  "title": "Chapter 47: Reserve Bank of India (RBI)",
  "order": 47,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qhqn8tn",
      "content": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) is the central bank of India. It regulates the country's monetary system and manages the currency and credit system of the economy. It plays a vital role in maintaining financial stability and controlling inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
