            "<p><strong>Function</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Issuer of Currency</p>",
            "<p>RBI issues currency notes except one-rupee note.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Banker to Government</p>",
            "<p>RBI manages accounts of central and state governments.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Banker's Bank</p>",
            "<p>Commercial banks keep reserves with RBI.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Controller of Credit</p>",
            "<p>RBI controls credit through monetary policy.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Custodian of Foreign Exchange</p>",
            "<p>RBI manages foreign exchange reserves.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Clearing House</p>",
            "<p>RBI settles interbank payments.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dc9vn61",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Monetary Policy Tools"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "85xsgjl",
      "content": "• Repo Rate – Rate at which RBI lends money to commercial banks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uia9xwt",
      "content": "• Reverse Repo Rate – Rate at which RBI borrows money from banks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wap9cy9",
      "content": "• Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR) – Percentage of deposits banks must keep with RBI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7d2vvrd",
      "content": "• Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR) – Percentage of deposits banks must maintain in liquid assets."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Quantitative Instruments",
        "Qualitative Instruments"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Repo Rate & Reverse Repo Rate",
          "Margin Requirements"
        ],
        [
          "Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)",
          "Moral Suasion"
        ],
        [
          "Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR)",
          "Selective Credit Control"
        ],
        [
          "Open Market Operations (OMO)",
          "Direct Action"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "ohf05pw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sv7o2i6",
      "content": "• Open Market Operations – Buying and selling government securities."
    },
    {
      "id": "n3g30so",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Organization of RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pi0o2da",
      "content": "• Governor – Head of RBI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0h5vav4",
      "content": "• Deputy Governors – Assist the Governor."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bjxtd9m",
      "content": "• Central Board of Directors – Governing body."
    },
    {
      "id": "vngfihl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Importance of RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "geft2q6",
      "content": "• Maintains financial stability."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9y18ipy",
      "content": "• Controls inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dgt4y1a",
      "content": "• Supervises banking system."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sir Osborne Smith was the first Governor of RBI, while C.D. Deshmukh was the first Indian Governor.",
        "The RBI's original headquarters was in Kolkata, which was permanently moved to Mumbai in 1937.",
        "One-rupee notes and coins are issued by the Ministry of Finance, signed by the Finance Secretary, not the RBI Governor."
      ],
      "id": "9550aqi"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n24a5jr",
      "content": "• Promotes economic development."
    },
